    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm seeing some weirdness in the datasets though—we've got these sudden, sharp spikes in salinity that don't seem to align with the temperature fluctuations or the local current models. It looks almost like sensor noise or some kind of intermittent glitching in the AUV's conductivity sensors. What's the best way to differentiate between actual localized salinity anomalies and technical sensor errors in these deep-sea profiles?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
