      "content": "Erratic and jittery data can sometimes be indicative of electronics interference, grounding issues, or internal communication glitches. Run a comprehensive self-diagnostic on the AUV to check all onboard systems and connections. You should also examine the electromagnetic environment. Unusual behavior might be related to submarine wireless communication disruptions or electrical noise from the AUV's own systems, such as those powering the conductivity sensor. Shielding the sensor or routing cables away from potential interference sources could mitigate these issues. Look into the AUV's serial communication logs for patterns correlating with the spikes, which might pinpoint the cause. If the issue persists, it may require more in-depth hardware troubleshooting or a consultation with the manufacturer’s technical support team.",
